From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] llama: load-time Q6_K requantization of the UD Q8_0 projection upcasts

The unsloth UD-Q4_K_M export upcasts the whole qwen35moe GDN/attention
projection stack to Q8_0 (~1.49 GB of weight reads per decoded token,
39.7% of decode kernel time, already at 76-87% of the R9700's bandwidth
ceiling). Requantize attn_qkv, attn_gate, ssm_out, attn_q and attn_output
to Q6_K while the model loads: ~300 MB/token of traffic removed, decode
106.5 -> 111.3 tok/s (+4.5%) same-binary. Gate-corpus ppl 3.931-3.947
across 10 runs (stock 3.9314, bound 3.9511) - the requantized weights are
byte-identical across loads (FNV-checksummed); the residual spread is
GPU-side accumulation-order noise also present at +/-0.01% on the
unmodified build. The shared-expert mats are deliberately excluded
(+0.5% ppl AND slower). GGML_LOAD_REQUANT=0 restores byte-identical
stock loading; GGML_LOAD_REQUANT_NTHREAD / _CSUM are debug toggles.

---
